'''''Adenocarpus hispanicus''''' is a species of [[flowering plant]] in the [[Faboideae]] subfamily that is endemic to the [[Iberian Peninsula]] in [[Spain]] and [[Portugal]]. It is {{convert|4|m}} high with its leaves being {{convert|2,5|-|7.5|mm}} long.<ref>{{cite journal|url=http://www.floravascular.com/index.php?spp=Adenocarpus%20argyrophyllus|title=Adenocarpus argyrophyllus (Rivas Goday) Caball.|volume=7|page=648|year=1948|publisher=Flora Vascular|place=Madrid}}</ref>

